For an accessibility tree update, Ladybird posts no notification at
all — and never AXLayoutChanged. Chrome never posts AXLayoutChanged
either: BrowserAccessibilityManagerMac::FireGeneratedEvent() maps
tree events to specific notifications (value, live-region, and focus
changes, e.g.), none of them a layout notification. Gecko and WebKit
post AXLayoutComplete only when an iframe’s document finishes loading:
Gecko from MOXWebAreaAccessible’s handleAccessibleEvent: for an
EVENT_DOCUMENT_LOAD_COMPLETE on a document that isn’t top-level, and
WebKit from AXObjectCache::onNonTopDocumentLoaded(). That fits what
VoiceOver did with Ladybird’s AXLayoutChanged on the scroll area holding
the AXWebArea: It treated the web area as a frame that had just loaded,
announcing a “frame” and moving into it.
